abstract: >-
  An accurate correction is not necessarily an adequate explanation, and an
  adequate explanation does not by itself mean that the person receiving it
  can evaluate it. This paper develops a normative account of explanatory
  authority, authority over where a difficulty is taken to lie, using
  second-language speaking as its principal case, and proposes a criterion
  for teaching, listeners and AI language tools.
